#!RuleTest
#test DRAFT-900045 expect=skipped domain=DS
#note "The discriminator that keeps the family from double-reporting: the DSSCAT column EXISTS (blank on both duplicated records), so Requirements.Variables.None [DSSCAT] skips this sister with a reason naming the column, and the parent DRAFT-900043 owns the case -- its All gate is satisfied by the same present column, and it reports each offending row with its location (see its invalid_dsscat_blank scenario over this same dataset)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DS class=EVENTS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSCAT    type=Char label="Category for Disposition Event"
col DSSCAT   type=Char label="Subcategory for Disposition Event"
col EPOCH    type=Char label="Epoch"
---
S1 | DS | 001 | 1 | DISPOSITION EVENT |  | TREATMENT
S1 | DS | 001 | 2 | DISPOSITION EVENT |  | TREATMENT
